  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mississippi received $5.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government awarded 79,833 contracts in the state, with an average award size of $69.3K. Obligations fell 30.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer in the state, obligating $4.8B. HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED is the largest contractor in Mississippi, receiving $3.5B in obligations. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations in the state, accounting for $3.6B. Other sizable industries include Other Support Activities for Air Transportation with $479M and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction with $139M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date rather than a full year. Historic fiscal-year obligations show variation: FY21 was $4.9B, FY22 was $5B, FY23 was $8.7B, FY24 was $6.5B, and FY25 was $8B. Buyers beyond the Department of Defense include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $278M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $137M. Top vendors beyond HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED include V2X AEROSPACE LLC at $437M and NOVA SPACE SOLUTIONS, LLC at $80.6M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are federal obligations in Mississippi?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense dominated FY2026 to date obligations with $4.8B. Ship Building and Repairing concentrated obligations at $3.6B, and HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED alone received $3.5B, showing high concentration in defense and shipbuilding. The rest of the market is smaller: the next-largest buyer, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, obligated $278M, and the second-largest vendor, V2X AEROSPACE LLC, received $437M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year and how does FY2026 compare to prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 30.9% year over year in FY2026 to date. FY26 obligations of $5.5B are lower than FY25 obligations of $8B and FY23 obligations of $8.7B, but higher than FY21 obligations of $4.9B and FY22 obligations of $5B. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $69.3K across 79,833 awards."
      }
    ]
  },
